fortnight is back and making a splash  with season three splashdown with all  the commotion over figuring out just  exactly what is new for players when  they log in we quickly go over the six  biggest changes in Chapter two season  three  a new season means a new map and  although you may recognize most of the  areas a significant portion of the map  is now underwater areas that were  previously at sea level are now  completely swamped or left in shambles  like the rickety rig and the fertility  meanwhile though situated at a higher  elevation remain comfortably safe which  means you won't have to be scrambling to  find a boat to navigate around retail  row or lazy Lakes  the next significant change is the  introduction of loot sharks and yes you  heard me correctly loot sharks are these  massive tanky sharks that swim around  the flooded areas will aggressively  pursue you if you're standing close to  the edge of the water trust us the first  time one came flying out of the water to  slide across a wooden deck to try and  tear us apart we were pretty shocked too  the good thing about these loot sharks  though is as their name implies they go  around eating up all the loot left  behind in the water so it's potentially  worth taking them out in order to get  what they've got hold up a fun thing you  can do is even use a fishing pole to  bait the shark and use it as a means to  traverse across the water even faster  now last season we had Deadpool  challenges but this season we have  something even better Jason Momoa the  Aquaman you know and love is now the  featured skin in season 3 he will have  his own set of challenges separate from  the general weekly set and completing  all of them throughout the course of the  season will net you not just as  Aquaman's skin but an Arthur curry  variant as well we also get one brand  new weapon and the return of an old  favorite the charged shotgun and the  hunting rifle the charged shotgun has  three in the chamber before you're  forced to reload so you can hold down  the trigger in order to give the gun  more punch in its shot while tightening  the spread and reducing recoil meanwhile  the hunting rifle a bolt-action weapon  without a scope that packs a serious  punch returns from the vault we're all  ready we're getting reactions from some  of fortnight's streamers on his return  most of them favorable this season three  a new battle pass makes his debut and  all the themed banner scans and gliders  reflect the changes to the season but  there seems to be a mix of older skins  as well as you level up the battle pass  you can continue to grind out XP to  unlock more  variance to make unassuming skins look  even better there's also a lore theme  with some of the skins being connected  to characters from season two so just  get the robot using kitten who's  following in his dad's footsteps  lastly the central hub with all of the  challenges and seasonal goodies has been  overhauled challenges are now in three  sets with general weekly challenges  style challenges and Aquaman challenges  all coming together to ensure that  players always have something to grind  for in order to receive XP or cosmetic  rewards you can even design the victory  umbrella glider with the Builder Brella  feature certain rewards in the battle  path will unlock upgrades to the shaft  canopy and even trail effects to really  set your creative flair and make the  victory umbrella your own there sure to  be more limited time modes and other  surprises throughout the season and  we're excited to see what port Knight  has up its sleeve let us know in the  comments below if you think the new  direction of fortnight season 3  splashdown theme is interesting or if  you preferred the days of the agency  we'll be putting out weekly guides to  help those of you looking to complete  the more difficult weekly challenges so  stay tuned to game spot  [Music]  you
 

